# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Tall Man), edited. The Tall Man: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_tall_man_arrived
Narrator: At the edge of the logging camp, the healed forest grows thick and green around the clear, bubbling Wellspring, though every trunk leans slightly the same way.
check Wisdom DC 18 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You keep close to the warm pool of your lantern light, and the hungry whispers of the dark slide harmlessly past your shoulders.
set mf_tall_man_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: A cold, heavy dread settles into {name}'s bones among the trees; their hands tremble, and for a long, miserable hour nothing goes right.
damage 2d10 psychic party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You walk beneath the green boughs of the healed forest, and every trunk you pass seems to have turned just an inch to watch your backs.
time +60
check Wisdom DC 18 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_bram_logger [afraid]: Folk keep wandering out of their tents in their nightshirts, walking straight into the trees. The few we find come back screaming, and none of them can say why.
set mf_tall_man_asked
quest mf_tall_man asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_bram_logger [weary]: Two more lads walked into the dark last night while we kept watch. Have you got any answer for this, or are we just waiting our turn?
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_tall_man_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_bram_logger [afraid]: Every hour you spend under those boughs, the dread gets heavier in your chest. Shadows stand right up off the moss to walk, and voices call from empty clearings.
-> menu

~ where
mf_bram_logger [sad]: You healed this wood for us, made the leaves come back green and sweet. Then the moon shrieked, and something long and thin walked out of the old fey ruins.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_bram_logger [neutral]: Old Hesper sits by the cookfire all night telling stories about the Greenwood's lost court. If anyone has a name for what stalks the timber, it'll be her.
* [Arcana DC 18] Hear the crone's tale and test it against the lore -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Persuasion DC 18] Ask for the old court's story in careful words -> a_ok | a_slow
* Sit by her fire all night and let her talk it out -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_bram_logger [smile]: Her old tale rings true enough to bet our necks on: a graceful lord of the Greenwood, rotted by neglect into the Tall Man, still pacing his ruined halls.
time +60
set mf_tall_man_found
set mf_tall_man_clue_a
quest mf_tall_man trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: You sit by the dying embers through a long, rambling night of old stories, until near dawn her cracked voice finally names the palace and the thing inside it.
time +300
set mf_tall_man_found
quest mf_tall_man trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: Sixty years I've told the tale of the Greenwood lord to anyone with ears, and nobody paid this old woman a copper of heed until the moon started falling!
set mf_tall_man_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_hesper_crone [neutral]: Come back to the fire and warm your hands, travelers. Ask what you need before the trees lean any closer.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_tall_man_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_tall_man_found and not flag.mf_tall_man_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: Before the rot took him, the Tall Man was a proud archfey with a court of fine dancers. Now he waits in his broken palace, starving for our fear.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: He comes to a frightened heart the way a moth comes to a tallow candle. Let him smell your terror in the brush, and you can lead him right home.
* [Survival DC 18] Stalk the woods and lure him with fear -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Intimidation DC 18] Make yourselves loud with dread and be hunted -> b_ok | b_slow
* Walk the woods all night frightened on purpose -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: That's the way of it: let him unfold those long limbs behind you, and coax him step by step back inside his own grey palace walls.
time +60
set mf_tall_man_found
set mf_tall_man_clue_b
quest mf_tall_man trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: You blunder through the tangled dark for half the night, heart in your throat, before something impossibly tall finally catches the scent of your fear and follows.
time +300
set mf_tall_man_found
quest mf_tall_man trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: Learn the steps of his lost court's measure, just as they danced it when the boughs were young. Dance it before his eyes, and the old Greenwood magic will scald him.
* [Performance DC 20] Learn the steps of the lost court dance -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [History DC 18] Study the old dance from her fingers' counting -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Practise the steps clumsily until dawn -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_hesper_crone [smile]: Watch my hand on my knee: tap, tap, turn, six measures round and a low courtly bow. You've got the rhythm in your heels now, dance for a vanished house.
time +60
give mf_court_notes
set mf_tall_man_weak
quest mf_tall_man ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: You stumble through the courtly steps on the damp moss until the sun that never rises would have cleared the trees, and at last the measure holds true.
time +300
give mf_court_notes
set mf_tall_man_weak
quest mf_tall_man ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: Ahead through the leaning trunks rises the ruined palace of the Greenwood court, its grey stone pillars cracked and its great roofless hall gaping open to the night.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_tall_man_reveals
Narrator: The Tall Man unfolds himself from between the grey pillars, impossibly thin and high, his crownless head bowed low beneath the roof where he once ruled as lord.
cutscene mf_tall_man_reveals_2
Narrator: He stretches out one long, jointed hand, and the cold shadows along the flagstones peel themselves off the ground to follow his fingers.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_tall_man_weak
combat mf_tall_man_weak
elif level >= 15
combat mf_tall_man_full
else
combat mf_tall_man_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_tall_man_falls
Narrator: With a dry creak like splitting timber, the Tall Man folds in upon himself, collapsing like a dropped puppet while the risen shadows sink flat against the stones.
cutscene mf_tall_man_falls_2
Narrator: High above the quiet canopy, the crone's face in the moon turns slowly northward, fixing her pale gaze upon the snows of the Howlers.
cutscene end
set mf_tall_man_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give hook_of_the_tall_man
quest mf_tall_man slain
xp milestone
Narrator: High on the frozen ridges of the Howlers, a shelf of loose shale slides into the gorge, and something vast turns over in the dark.
-> END
